        "text": "Using a 10-step monthly binomial lattice:\n\n- Time step: \\(\\Delta t = 1/12\\)\n- Volatility: \\(\\sigma = 0.20\\)\n- Risk-free rate: \\(r = 0.10\\)\n- Strike: \\(K = 14\\)\n- Initial stock price: \\(S_0 = 12\\)\n\nFor a Cox-Ross-Rubinstein binomial tree:\n\n\\[\nu = e^{\\sigma\\sqrt{\\Delta t}} = e^{0.20\\sqrt{1/12}} \\approx 1.05943\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = e^{-\\sigma\\sqrt{\\Delta t}} \\approx 0.94390\n\\]\n\nRisk-neutral probability:\n\n\\[\np = \\frac{e^{r\\Delta t}-d}{u-d}\n= \\frac{e^{0.10/12}-0.94390}{1.05943-0.94390}\n\\approx 0.558\n\\]\n\nThe call is in the money at maturity only for sufficiently high terminal stock prices. Computing the terminal payoffs and discounting the risk-neutral expected payoff gives approximately:\n\n\\[\nC_0 \\approx 0.53\n\\]\n\nSo the option price is about **53 cents**, corresponding to choice **F**.\n\nAnswer: F",
