        "text": "For a reversible adiabatic process, \\(q = 0\\).\n\nFor a monoatomic ideal gas:\n\n\\[\nC_V = \\frac{3}{2}R,\\qquad C_P = \\frac{5}{2}R,\\qquad \\gamma = \\frac{5}{3}\n\\]\n\nInitial temperature:\n\n\\[\nT_1 = 45^\\circ\\text{C} = 318.15\\ \\text{K}\n\\]\n\nFor reversible adiabatic expansion/compression:\n\n\\[\nT_1V_1^{\\gamma-1}=T_2V_2^{\\gamma-1}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nT_2 = T_1\\left(\\frac{V_1}{V_2}\\right)^{\\gamma-1}\n=318.15\\left(\\frac{75}{20}\\right)^{2/3}\n\\approx 767.8\\ \\text{K}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\Delta T = 767.8 - 318.15 \\approx 449.65\\ \\text{K}\n\\]\n\nChange in internal energy:\n\n\\[\n\\Delta E = nC_V\\Delta T\n=2\\left(\\frac{3}{2}R\\right)(449.65)\n\\approx 11.21\\ \\text{kJ}\n\\]\n\nChange in enthalpy:\n\n\\[\n\\Delta H = nC_P\\Delta T\n=2\\left(\\frac{5}{2}R\\right)(449.65)\n\\approx 18.68\\ \\text{kJ}\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\nq=0,\\quad \\Delta E=11.21\\ \\text{kJ},\\quad \\Delta H=18.68\\ \\text{kJ}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: E",
