        "text": "For laminar flow, the head loss is\n\n\\[\nh_f=\\frac{32\\mu L V}{\\rho g D^2}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\n\\[\nD=\\frac{1/4}{12}=0.02083\\text{ ft}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mu=0.679\\times10^{-3}\\text{ lbm/ft-s}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nL=16\\text{ ft}\n\\]\n\nCritical velocity occurs at \\(Re=2500\\):\n\n\\[\nV_c=\\frac{Re\\mu}{\\rho D}\n\\]\n\nUsing \\(\\rho=62.4\\text{ lbm/ft}^3\\):\n\n\\[\nV_c=\\frac{2500(0.679\\times10^{-3})}{62.4(0.02083)}\n\\approx 1.306\\text{ ft/s}\n\\]\n\nFlow velocity is half critical:\n\n\\[\nV=\\frac{V_c}{2}\\approx 0.653\\text{ ft/s}\n\\]\n\nNow compute head loss:\n\n\\[\nh_f=\\frac{32(0.679\\times10^{-3})(16)(0.653)}\n{62.4(32.2)(0.02083)^2}\n\\approx 0.260\\text{ ft}\n\\]\n\nConvert to inches:\n\n\\[\n0.260\\times12\\approx 3.12\\text{ in}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: A",
